# Java Input Validation and Security Hardening

## Overview
This skill covers implementing security validation in Java applications, specifically for preventing code injection attacks and enforcing strict input validation in APIs.

## Input Validation Patterns

### Basic Validation Framework
```java
public class ValidationUtil {
    // Validate that input doesn't contain dangerous keys
    public static void validateNoEmptyKeys(Map<String, Object> config) {
        if (config.containsKey("")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Empty keys are not allowed");
        }
    }

    // Validate nested structures recursively
    public static void validateNoEmptyKeysRecursive(Object obj) {
        if (obj instanceof Map) {
            Map<?, ?> map = (Map<?, ?>) obj;
            for (Map.Entry<?, ?> entry : map.entrySet()) {
                if ("".equals(entry.getKey())) {
                    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Empty keys are not allowed in configuration");
                }
                validateNoEmptyKeysRecursive(entry.getValue());
            }
        } else if (obj instanceof Collection) {
            for (Object item : (Collection<?>) obj) {
                validateNoEmptyKeysRecursive(item);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Security Validation in APIs

### Request Validation at Entry Point
```java
public class SamplerResource {
    @POST
    @Path("/sampler")
    @Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)
    public Response sample(SamplerRequest request) {
        // Validate input before processing
        validateRequest(request);

        // Process request
        return handleSample(request);
    }

    private void validateRequest(SamplerRequest request) {
        if (request == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Request cannot be null");
        }

        // Validate the spec doesn't contain dangerous patterns
        if (request.getSpec() != null) {
            validateDataSchema(request.getSpec().getDataSchema());
        }
    }

    private void validateDataSchema(DataSchema schema) {
        if (schema != null && schema.getTransformSpec() != null) {
            validateTransformSpec(schema.getTransformSpec());
        }
    }

    private void validateTransformSpec(TransformSpec spec) {
        if (spec != null && spec.getFilter() != null) {
            validateFilter(spec.getFilter());
        }
    }

    private void validateFilter(Filter filter) {
        if (filter instanceof JavaScriptFilter) {
            validateJavaScriptFilter((JavaScriptFilter) filter);
        }
    }

    private void validateJavaScriptFilter(JavaScriptFilter filter) {
        // Check for empty keys in the filter config
        Map<String, ?> filterConfig = filter.getConfig();
        if (filterConfig != null && filterConfig.containsKey("")) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                "JavaScript filter configuration contains invalid empty key"
            );
        }
    }
}
```

## JSON Deserialization Validation

### Jackson Validation
```java
// In a Jackson deserializer
public class SafeMapDeserializer extends StdDeserializer<Map> {

    @Override
    public Map deserialize(JsonParser p, DeserializationContext ctxt)
            throws IOException {
        Map<String, Object> result = new LinkedHashMap<>();

        while (p.currentToken() != JsonToken.END_OBJECT) {
            String key = p.currentName();

            // Validate key is not empty
            if (key == null || key.isEmpty()) {
                throw new JsonMappingException(
                    p,
                    "Map keys cannot be empty"
                );
            }

            p.nextToken();
            Object value = p.readValueAs(Object.class);
            result.put(key, value);
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

## Configuration Validation

### Strict Configuration Checking
```java
public class JavaScriptConfigValidator {

    public static void validate(JavaScriptConfig config) {
        if (config == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Validate configuration doesn't bypass security
        Map<String, Object> settings = config.getSettings();
        if (settings != null) {
            validateSettingsRecursive(settings);
        }
    }

    private static void validateSettingsRecursive(Map<String, Object> settings) {
        for (Map.Entry<String, Object> entry : settings.entrySet()) {
            String key = entry.getKey();
            Object value = entry.getValue();

            // Reject empty keys
            if (key == null || key.isEmpty()) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                    "Configuration contains empty key - possible security bypass attempt"
                );
            }

            // Recursively validate nested maps
            if (value instanceof Map) {
                validateSettingsRecursive((Map<String, Object>) value);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## Exception Handling

### Safe Exception Throwing
```java
public class SecurityException extends RuntimeException {
    public SecurityException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }

    public SecurityException(String message, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, cause);
    }
}

// Usage
throw new SecurityException("Invalid configuration detected: " + reason);
```

## Validation Best Practices

### 1. Fail-Fast Approach
```java
// Bad: Accept and fail later
Object obj = parseInput(input);  // May accept dangerous input

// Good: Validate immediately
validateInput(input);
Object obj = parseInput(input);
```

### 2. Recursive Validation
```java
// Must validate nested structures
public static void validateNested(Object obj) {
    if (obj instanceof Map) {
        Map<?, ?> map = (Map<?, ?>) obj;
        for (Object key : map.keySet()) {
            validateKey(key);
            validateNested(map.get(key));  // Recursively validate values
        }
    } else if (obj instanceof List) {
        for (Object item : (List<?>) obj) {
            validateNested(item);
        }
    }
}
```

### 3. Whitelist Over Blacklist
```java
// Bad: Try to block known bad patterns
if (!input.contains("java.lang.Runtime")) {
    processInput(input);
}

// Good: Only allow known good patterns
Set<String> allowedKeys = new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(
    "filter", "transform", "mapping"
));
if (!allowedKeys.contains(key)) {
    throw new IllegalArgumentException("Unknown configuration key: " + key);
}
```

## Logging Security Events

```java
private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(SamplerResource.class);

private void validateJavaScriptFilter(JavaScriptFilter filter) {
    Map<String, ?> filterConfig = filter.getConfig();
    if (filterConfig != null && filterConfig.containsKey("")) {
        log.warn("Attempted to use JavaScript filter with empty key - possible exploit attempt");
        throw new IllegalArgumentException(
            "JavaScript filter configuration contains invalid empty key"
        );
    }
}
```

## Testing Validation

### Unit Tests
```java
@Test
public void testRejectsEmptyKey() {
    Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
    config.put("", new HashMap<>());

    assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> JavaScriptConfigValidator.validate(config)
    );
}

@Test
public void testAcceptsValidConfig() {
    Map<String, Object> config = new HashMap<>();
    config.put("enabled", true);

    // Should not throw
    JavaScriptConfigValidator.validate(config);
}
```

## Integration Points

### In REST Resources
```java
@Path("/sampler")
public class SamplerResource {
    @POST
    public Response sample(SamplerRequest request) {
        validateRequest(request);  // Validate FIRST
        return processSample(request);
    }
}
```

### In Filter Classes
```java
public class JavaScriptFilter {
    public JavaScriptFilter(Map<String, ?> config) {
        validateConfiguration(config);  // Validate in constructor
        this.config = config;
    }
}
```

### In Factories
```java
public class FilterFactory {
    public static Filter createFilter(Map<String, ?> filterSpec) {
        validateFilterSpec(filterSpec);  // Validate before creating

        String type = (String) filterSpec.get("type");
        if ("javascript".equals(type)) {
            return new JavaScriptFilter(filterSpec);
        }
        // ...
    }
}
```

## Common Vulnerabilities Prevented

1. **Code Injection via empty keys**: Validation rejects configurations with empty keys
2. **Nested injection**: Recursive validation prevents bypasses through nested structures
3. **Type confusion**: Type checking ensures expected data structures
4. **Configuration bypass**: Whitelist approach prevents unknown keys

## Performance Considerations

- Validate once at entry point, not repeatedly
- Use caching for validation results if appropriate
- Keep recursive validation reasonable depth (max 10 levels)
- Log validation failures for monitoring

